 1. What DeepClaim is
DeepClaim is an AI agent for Indian hospitals that reads their bills, insurance claims and settlements, and shows the owner exactly where insurance money is lost: which insurers and procedures pay below cost, which claim cuts the hospital itself absorbs, and which of those can be prevented or recovered. Owners and finance heads can ask questions on WhatsApp, in English, Tamil or Hindi, and get answers traced back to the actual bills.
The promise in one line: find the insurance money your hospital is leaving on the table, and get the part that's yours back.
What it does (the five jobs)
Job	What the hospital gets
See	Profit for each procedure, for each payer (each insurer, government scheme and cash), using the hospital's own costs.
Stop	Every bill is checked against the rate agreed with that insurer before it is sent, so cuts the hospital can't pass on are avoided.
Recover	Cuts the hospital absorbs (short settlements after discharge, scheme deductions) are flagged, and an appeal is drafted for staff to review and send.
Negotiate	Before each insurer renewal, a ready evidence pack: which procedures lose money with that insurer, volumes sent, and a proposed rate card.
Ask	Plain-language answers on WhatsApp, plus a daily summary. Every number links back to the source bills.

