3. The problem: "Where the money slips away"
SECTION HEADLINE
Not every insurance cut is your loss. Some are, and nobody is tracking them.
CARD 1 · RATES THAT DON'T COVER COST
Package rates have barely moved while your costs rose. Some procedures may be losing money with some payers, and today nobody can tell you which.
CARD 2 · CUTS AFTER THE PATIENT GOES HOME
Insurers can settle below the approved amount weeks after discharge. That's why some hospitals hold a 5–10% deposit. When the cut is bigger, you're chasing a patient who has already left.
CARD 3 · BILLS ABOVE THE AGREED TARIFF
If a bill crosses the rate you agreed with the insurer, the excess is cut and can't be charged to the patient. Usually it's a billing mistake that could have been caught.
CARD 4 · SCHEME DEDUCTIONS
Under PM-JAY and other schemes, patients can't be asked to pay. Every rupee deducted is yours to absorb.
CARD 5 · MONEY WAITING
Cashless means you fund the treatment until the insurer pays. Every extra week of waiting is working capital you can't use.
4. How it works (four steps, with icons)
STEP 1 · CONNECT
Share the exports you already have: bills, claim and settlement statements, bank credits, your agreed tariffs. No new software for your staff.
