Layout, imagery and motion
•	Layout: generous white space; 12-column grid, max content width about 1,200px; sections alternate Paper and Ink Navy. Big numbers, short paragraphs.
•	Signature visual: the animated claim bill (hero), reused in small form across the site as the brand motif.
•	Imagery: real product views (WhatsApp chat, worklist, margin card) in clean phone and laptop frames; simple line icons; data charts in the brand colours. If photos are used, they should be original photos of Indian hospital billing and insurance desks, not stock.
•	Motion: subtle and purposeful: numbers count up when they scroll into view, bill lines highlight in sequence, charts draw in. Respect the visitor's 'reduce motion' setting.
•	Mobile first: most owners will open the link on WhatsApp on their phone. Test every section at 375px width; keep the sticky 'Book audit' and WhatsApp buttons.
•	Accessibility: WCAG AA contrast, minimum 16px text, keyboard-friendly calculator and form, alt text on all visuals.
Logo direction
•	Wordmark "DeepClaim" in Fraunces or a custom geometric sans, Ink Navy.
•	Symbol idea: a folded claim document whose lower corner reveals a deeper layer in Ledger Teal ("reading beneath the claim"), or a lens over a ruled line.
•	Must work in one colour, at favicon size, and on WhatsApp profile images.
Alternative theme (if you want something lighter)
"Clinical Clear": all-white background, a single cobalt accent (#2347D6), Inter throughout, IBM Plex Mono for numbers. Safer and more conventional, but less memorable. I recommend Deep Ledger.

